cause I just don't think the market is, like I think the market is at the stage that is not, highly likely to get a multi-week or multi-month rally or a stage to uptrend. So where, yeah, so I think the stage of the market is or like the situation of awareness is pretty important. And the second factor is definitely my my own equity curve, like whether I'm doing well or not in the past, in the recent sessions. So generally I will be less willing to take profits. I will be holding more, holding a larger positions to capture a larger move when I'm doing well, when I'm trading well. Compared to when I just suffer from a drawdown, then probably I will be more willing to take more profits and protect my positions, like to raise my stock to break even, etc. Yeah, I think I... my entry. Yeah, but limits all the guard fields, but... My entry is around like 182.30ish. Original one is like 18ish, but it's just a few cents away from my limit order. So a little bit unfortunate, but that's fine. Yeah, but definitely the best entry will be the breakdown of this five minute candle. Actually, even if you use the breakdown of the 15 minute counter, it's still like less than 1.5% to stop. And it's really tight. But I just trying to push the limit a little bit further. Yeah. I don't think setting stops, getting two types, setting two types is really a good thing. It really depends on your style and how you handle it. Again, don't blindly copy be my style, entries, stop placements, stop selection, et cetera. And also, and the semi-short is also another like a pretty huge position. on it that I've talked recently. And it's after the SNDK back.",
